infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Eager list vs lazy generator: collect or stream?
  desc Reuse, length, indexing -> list. Big, one-pass, flat memory -> generator.
  compares
    - label Eager list [ ... ]
      children
        - label Need it more than once
          desc Reuse the result without rebuilding it
        - label Need its length
          desc len() requires the whole thing stored
        - label Need indexing
          desc Random access by position, result[i]
    - label Lazy generator ( ... )
      children
        - label Large or unbounded input
          desc 50 GB file, infinite stream
        - label Single pass only
          desc One-shot iterator, empty after consuming
        - label Memory stays flat
          desc One value at a time, constant RAM
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
